.TH UNITOTEM-MANAGER 8 "October 2026" "unitotem-manager" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
unitotem-manager \- UniTotem kiosk scheduler and web management interface
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B unitotem-manager
[\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Starts the scheduler, the HTTPS API with the web interface (ports 443, and 80 redirecting to it) and, when
unitotem-viewer is installed and a display is available, one viewer window per screen. It is normally started
by the unitotem-manager.service unit.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-no_gui true
Headless: run only the backend, without the local windows.
.SH ACCOUNTS
The accounts of the web interface are the accounts of the operating system: the user name and password are checked by PAM
(service
.IR unitotem-manager ),
and only root and the members of the group
.I unitotem
may log in. A user created in the web interface is created on the system and added to that group; its capabilities
(scheduler, audio, power, admin) are kept by UniTotem. The users and their passwords (as the system keeps them) are part
of the backup.
.SH FIRST ACCESS
Until an administrator exists the web interface only offers the setup page, where the person chooses the username and
password of the first administrator (a new system account in the group). The welcome screen of the device shows its
address. Resetting the users from the backup page returns the node to this state.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/unitotem
Configuration, playlists, users and pairing data.
.TP
.I /var/lib/unitotem/uploaded
Uploaded files.
.TP
.I /etc/ssl/unitotem.pem
Certificate and key of the web interface, created at installation.
.SH SEE ALSO
https://github.com/a13ssandr0/unitotem-manager
